      "content": "Here's an expanded version:\n\nWelcome to CloudScale, a modern API platform for building scalable and secure applications. To get started, you'll need to authenticate your request and set up the necessary headers for your API call.\n\nFirst, you'll need to obtain an API key with the required permissions. This can be done by creating a new account on our website or by using an existing credentials method that works for your organization. Once you have your API key, you can make an initial request to initiate the background monitoring process.\n\n**Initial Request Setup**\n\nTo send an initial request, you'll need to make a POST request to `https://api.cloudscale.io/v1/auth/init`. Your request should contain the following information:\n\n- `Content-Type: application/json`\n- `X-Api-Key (API Key)`: This header is a string that identifies your request as legitimate and allows us to authenticate and authorize your access.\n- `Authorization: Bearer (no authorization header, as this is an initialization request)`\n\nThe initial request should include a JSON payload with the following structure:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"api_key\": \"(Your API Key)\",\n  \"organization\": \"(Your Organization ID)\"\n}\n```\n\nWhen you make this initial request, you",
